<title>GERMANY: Siemens wins Philippine power station order.</title>
<headline>Siemens wins Philippine power station order.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electrical and electronics group Siemens AG said on Tuesday it had won a contract to build a power station worth about one billion marks in the Philippines.  </p>
<p>Siemens power station subsidiary KWU said a preliminary contract had been signed on Tuesday during a visit to the Philippines by German Chancellor Helmut Kohl.</p>
<p>The contract to build the gas and steam turbine power station was awarded by First Gas Power Station Corporation, a joint venture between First Philippine Holdings Corp and British Gas Plc.</p>
<p>The contract comprises the construction of the plant and its operation for six years, KWU said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
